            "name": "Analytic 2092",
            "description": "Real-time monitoring identifies wscript.exe/cscript.exe/mshta.exe or other JScript execution from unexpected parents/paths, especially when followed by child interpreters, network connections, or system modification. Alert only when the interpreter is not part of the asset's approved software/automation baseline or its execution context violates an approved signer/hash/path/parent/user rule, and require OT-relevant corroboration such as access to engineering files, ICS software/API use, communications with protected OT assets, configuration change, or another suspicious follow-on behavior. Suppress documented vendor software, engineering workflows, diagnostics, backup, patching, and approved maintenance. ",
